course: dictionary
lesson: 6200
title: Reading the right way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To misread means to read something wrongly. You can misread words, signs, maps, times, and even people. «Picture signs are still misread today.» Look at the prefix: mis- means wrongly, so misread means read wrongly.
explain: To misread a situation or a person means to understand them wrongly. In a story, a character might misread someone's feelings and cause a problem. The clues in the words and pictures around you help you check that you have understood them correctly.
explain: In school, misreading a question is a common reason for losing marks. Reading «add» as «subtract» changes the whole answer. Tip: read the question twice and underline the key words before you start.
fact: Misread is a verb. Its past forms are spelt the same: misread, misreads, misread, misreading.
fact: The past form «misread» is said «mis-RED», so it sounds like the colour red.
fact: «Mis-» means wrongly, as in misread, misspell and misbehave.
fact: Misreading a question is a common reason for losing marks, for example reading «add» as «subtract».
fact: Read the question twice and underline the key words so you do not misread it.
exercise: «Picture signs are still misread today.» What does misread mean here? | Drawn again | Read aloud very clearly | Never read at all | *Read wrongly
exercise: In a test, Ayo reads «add» as «subtract». What has Ayo done? | Understood the question perfectly | Read the question out loud | Answered the question twice | *Misread the question
exercise: Which word uses mis- to mean wrongly? | preview | *misbehave | bicycle | submarine
test: What is the past form of misread said as? | mis-REED | *mis-RED | mis-RID | MIS-road
test: What does misreading a person mean? | Meeting them for the first time | Reading their name aloud | Writing a letter to them | *Understanding them wrongly
exam: Ella reads a map and goes the wrong way. What did she do? | Disagreed with the map | Previewed the map | *Misread the map | Redid the map
